---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Compliance — legal reverse engineering only | rea.run"
  description="rea.run publishes guides for authorized reverse engineering and security research only. No crack, keygen, or DRM circumvention content."
  path="/compliance/"
>
  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--color-ink)]">Compliance</h1>
    <p class="mt-4">This community site documents <strong>legal, authorized</strong> use of REA and related tools.</p>
    <h2>Allowed framing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Analyzing software you own, build, or have explicit permission to inspect.</li>
      <li>Security research and malware analysis under applicable law and contracts.</li>
      <li>Interoperability research where your jurisdiction permits it.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Not published here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Crack, keygen, license-bypass, or piracy instructions.</li>
      <li>DRM circumvention how-tos.</li>
      <li>Invented product prices or capabilities for REA or third parties.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Affiliation</h2>
    <p>rea.run is unofficial and not affiliated with morluto, Hex-Rays, the NSA/Ghidra project, or operators of other “REA” domains such as rea.tools. Upstream source of truth: <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea">github.com/morluto/rea</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
